# Shot O'Clock — Environment Variables Template
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values.
# Never commit `.env` to git. (Already in .gitignore.)
#
# Variables prefixed with EXPO_PUBLIC_ are exposed to the mobile app at runtime.
# Any value that should NOT reach the client (service role keys, server secrets)
# must NOT use the EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix.
#
# After editing .env, restart `npx expo start` for changes to take effect.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase (required for local dev)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The Supabase project URL.
# For local development: this is the URL printed by `supabase start`
# (typically http://127.0.0.1:54321). For production: the project URL
# from your Supabase dashboard.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321

# The Supabase anon (public) key for the project.
# Local: printed by `supabase start` under "anon key".
# Production: from your Supabase project's API settings.
# This key is safe to expose in the mobile app — it only grants the
# permissions defined by RLS policies.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJI...replace-me

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-only secrets (NEVER prefix with EXPO_PUBLIC_)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The service role key bypasses RLS entirely. Never put it in the mobile app.
# Only needed for:
#   - Local seeding scripts (supabase/seed.sql runs as service role automatically)
#   - Server-side functions you trigger manually
#
# For most MVP work you do NOT need this set. Leave commented unless you have
# a specific script that needs it.
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJI...replace-me

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Development conveniences (optional)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Toggle on to render extra debug UI in the mobile app (round numbers, phase
# state, etc.). Default off. Should never be true in production builds.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_DEBUG_OVERLAY=false

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Notes
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# - Production env vars are managed via EAS Build secrets, not this file.
#   See: https://docs.expo.dev/build-reference/variables/
#
# - When adding a new env var, update both this file AND `apps/mobile/src/lib/env.ts`
#   (the typed config loader) in the same commit. Untyped env access is forbidden.
#
# - Anything containing a secret, token, or password belongs in `.env`, NOT in
#   this template.
